{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 74,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Maskil of Asaph. Why have You rejected us forever, O God? Why does Your anger smolder against the sheep of Your pasture?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember Your congregation, which You purchased long ago and redeemed as the tribe of Your inheritance — Mount Zion, where You dwell.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Turn Your steps to the everlasting ruins, to everything in the sanctuary the enemy has destroyed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Your foes have roared within Your meeting place; they have unfurled their banners as signs,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "like men wielding axes in a thicket of trees",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and smashing all the carvings with hatchets and picks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have burned Your sanctuary to the ground; they have defiled the dwelling place of Your Name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They said in their hearts, “We will crush them completely.” They burned down every place where God met us in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There are no signs for us to see. There is no longer any prophet. And none of us knows how long this will last.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How long, O God, will the enemy taunt You? Will the foe revile Your name forever?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why do You withdraw Your strong right hand? Stretch it out to destroy them!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet God is my King from ancient times, working salvation on the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You divided the sea by Your strength; You smashed the heads of the dragons of the sea;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You crushed the heads of Leviathan; You fed him to the creatures of the desert.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You broke open the fountain and the flood; You dried up the ever-flowing rivers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The day is Yours, and also the night; You established the moon and the sun.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You set all the boundaries of the earth; You made the summer and winter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember how the enemy has mocked You, O LORD, how a foolish people has spurned Your name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not deliver the soul of Your dove to beasts; do not forget the lives of Your afflicted forever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Consider Your covenant, for haunts of violence fill the dark places of the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not let the oppressed retreat in shame; may the poor and needy praise Your name.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rise up, O God; defend Your cause! Remember how the fool mocks You all day long.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.74.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.74.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not disregard the clamor of Your adversaries, the uproar of Your enemies that ascends continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
